on\", \"authorization is merely a suggestion\", clues `inventory_route` + `protected_reference`, 403 `field_action_forbidden` | GET inventory -> every single field x action on the protected id | done; Mastery |\n| 39 | improper API inventory: shadow / old version / beta / debug endpoint without the check (API9) | gap | `/api/v1` vs `/v2`, `version`/`deprecated` keys in inventory or openapi, `X-API-Version`, \"legacy\", \"beta\", \"old docs\" | list every documented + version-swapped path, call the protected op on each | high |\n| 40 | unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (API4) | gap | `limit`/`page_size`/`per_page`, \"only shows 10\", rate-limit headers | `limit=100000`, `page=-1`, `per_page=0`, offset past the public window | med |\n| 10b | command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind / output-less, argument injection | gap | `invalid_characters`/`forbidden` on `;`, no `stdout` echo, \"ping\"/\"dig\"/\"tar\"/\"curl\" wrappers | `%0a`, `$(...)`, backticks, `${IFS}`, `-o`/`--output` argument flags, write proof into a served path, sleep only as a last resort | med-high (D16 sequel) |\n| 23b | GraphQL sequels: aliases/batching, mutations without authz, introspection off, GET/persisted queries | gap | `[{\"query\":..}]` arrays accepted, `mutation` type in schema, \"Did you mean\" suggestions, rate-limited field | alias the protected field N times, batched array, call the mutation, field-suggestion walk | med (D18 sequel) |\n| 27b | auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, reset link via Host header, token leaked in response, login state machine | gap | `/verify`, `otp_required`, `step: 2`, \"remember me\", reset email preview, `X-Forwarded-Host` in links | skip to the final step with the step-1 session, reuse/omit the code, Host-header poisoned link | high (D17 sibling) |\n| 41 | WebSocket / alternate-transport authz (CSWSH, per-message checks) | gap | `ws://`/`wss://` in JS, `Upgrade: websocket`, \"real-time\", \"socket\", \"channel\" | send the protected request over the socket (no per-message authz), cross-origin handshake | med-high (\"vary the protocol surface\") |\n| 42 | CRLF / response header injection | gap | a param reflected in `Location`/`Set-Cookie`, \"header\", \"newline\" | `%0d%0aSet-Cookie: role=admin`, `%0d%0a%0d%0a<body>` | med |\n| 44 | forged webhook / unsafe consumption of a \"trusted\" event (OWASP API10, A08) | seen D19 | \"believes every event it's told about\", \"forged news\", clues `event_type` + `owner_scope` (values), feature 405 `post_required`, POST -> `webhook_rejected`, `[]` -> 500 | ONE JSON body: clue values under every alias (`event_type`/`type`/`event`, `owner_scope`/`scope`/`owner`) + `role`/`current_role: admin` + `source`/`sender: provider` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted: true` -> `forged_event_consumed` | done; Mastery |\n| 44b | webhook sequels: HMAC signature with a leaked/weak secret, replayable timestamp, provider allowlist by header/IP | gap | `X-Hub-Signature-256`/`X-Signature`/`Stripe-Signature` named in errors (`signature_invalid`, `timestamp_expired`), a sample signed event in a guide/log | re-sign the forged body with the leaked secret (HMAC-SHA256 over raw body / `t.body`), replay a logged event with a new payload, provider header/IP spoof | high (D19 sequel) |\n| 45 | crypto failures: predictable / weak tokens, unsalted hashes, ECB/bit-flip cookies (OWASP A02) | gap | tokens = md5(username)/timestamp/sequential, hex digest of a known value, \"encrypted\" cookie whose blocks repeat, \"padding\" | derive the victim token from data the app shows; flip/cut-paste cookie blocks | med |\n| 46 | known-vulnerable component / version disclosure (OWASP A06) | gap | version banner/header (`X-Powered-By`, `/version`, footer), \"outdated\", \"unpatched\", a guide naming a library version | look up the documented weakness of that exact version (route/param), exploit the documented path only | low-med |\n| 47 | log injection / log forging / audit trail tampering (OWA