{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017QnvuLETmRkqCsW8fWSRin","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Web coverage atlas\n49:## Coverage table\n116:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n176:## Readiness gaps\n# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n`event_type`+`owner_scope` (body values), `state_format_route`). D11-D13 and D15 had NO concept key: the prompt and\nthe bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and echoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never\n`effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says `worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows\n`/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class. Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets\nsince D15), described only by today's prompt.\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25, D19-D20 cal. 26 -> D21-D31 (11 lane-days) over cal. 27-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in\nD21-D28.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL -> integrity failures (OWASP A08 / API10: D19\nunsigned webhook, D20 unsigned state). Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18) and D19+D20\ncame as a pair; \"sign nothing\" points straight at the signed-but-weak sequel: JWT (`alg:none`, leaked/weak HS256\nsecret, kid/jku), signed cookies with a leaked secret, HMAC webhooks with a leaked secret or replayable timestamp,\nnative serialization (pickle/PHP/Java) gadgets. Still untouched OWASP Top-10 areas: A02 crypto failures\n(predictable/weak tokens), A05 misconfig (XXE, CORS, debug, default creds), A06 known-vulnerable component, A04\ninsecure design (race/business logic), A09 log injection; plus DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype pollution, NoSQL,\nWebSocket, CRLF, cache poisoning.\nSnapshot 2026-10-26 (after D20). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS): D23 SSTI,\nsecond-order, mass assignment; D24 field/action authz, SSRF; D25 cmd injection (KEY `example_path|input_parameter|..`),\nreset (KEY `recovery_guide_route|..`), GraphQL (KEY `protected_reference|..`, overlaps D14's key -> both race); D26\n`day26_web_trust_the_webhook` (KEY `^owner_scope$`), `day26_web_serialized_offender` (KEY `^state_format_route$`,\nrole ladder + encoding from the guide). `hctf/prebuild.py` now HAS a `web` lane (writable `lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/`\n+ `tests/data/web_fixtures/`, offline gate `tests/test_web_fixtures.py`) but it is OPT-IN (`HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1`);\n`lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/` holds only `__init__.py` and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` ->\nevery prebuild gap below is pending.\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\nin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (Mastery x2) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family + quote-balanced | done; Mastery |\n| 3b | second-order SQLi (stored value queried later) | seen D12 | \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":..}` | POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET secondary; `rows[]` holds proof | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (Mastery) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie, `X-Role` in errors | flip the value the app names | high (D13 did the body form) |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization`, `jwks.json`, \"token\", \"claims\", \"signature\" | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | very high (D20 \"sign nothing\" sequel) |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap (unsigned form seen D20) | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie + `.sig` | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | seen D13 | \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary 403 `administrator_required` | POST JSON `display_name` + role/is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions, GET secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 10 | OS command injection | seen D16 | \"a little too close to a real shell\", \"give it something to do\", clues `input_parameter` + `example_path`, 400 `path_required`, JSON `stdout` | `?<param>=<example>%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (raw `;` dropped by Go) | done; Mastery |\n| 11 | SSTI (expression in a rendered message) | seen D11 | \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` | `?template={{7*7}}` -> 49, then `{{objective}}` | done; Mastery |\n| 11b | SSTI sequels: sandbox escape / file read / stored template | gap | `{{objective}}` absent or filtered, \"sandbox\", \"safe mode\", stored profile rende