{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TpUiUgaDryaxMKTQCSE8e2","type":"tool_result","content":"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D21-D28 at ~2-3 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\nstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\nraised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). Aft\n  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing a\n  {\"id\": \"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\", \"concept\": \"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a\n  {\"id\": \"webhook-signature-sequels\", \"concept\": \"webhook sequels: HMAC-signed events with a leaked/weak secret, replay, provider allowlist (row 44b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 'Trust the Webhook' was the unsigned form (clues event_type + owner_scope as body values; narrow bodies -> webhook_rejected; an alias-union JSON with role/source/trust flags -> forged_event_consumed). Signed sequel planner: read signature header names from errors/guides (X-Hub-Signature-256 'sha256=<hex>', X-Signature, X-Webhook-Signature, Stripe-Signature 't=..,v1=..', Svix 'v1,<b64>'), compu\n  {\"id\": \"alias-union-body-builder\", \"concept\": \"one JSON body carrying every clue value under every plausible alias + privilege/trust flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 lost ~60 s across three workers bisecting ~30 narrow bodies against a sink whose only error was webhook_rejected; the answer-first worker's kitchen-sink body landed first try in single/TT/Mastery. Pure builder: input = clue JSON (minus route keys) + optional guide sample; output = ordered list of JSON bodies: (1) union body: each value under its key and aliases (event_type/type/event/kind/action/topic/\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves \n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value lad\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 \n  {\"id\": \"websocket-authz\", \"concept\": \"WebSocket / alternate transport skips the REST authz (row 41)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18's prompt: 'Vary the protocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline' -- the same protected object reached via another transport. Planner: find ws:// / wss:// / socket.io / SSE / JSON-RPC endpoints in inline JS and clues; build the handshake (Origin same/foreign/null for CSWSH) and send the protected read (protected_reference) as a message; also JSON-RPC {method, params} over POST and REST<->GraphQL equivalents of t\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<all\n  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"native / signed serialization sequels: pickle, PHP, Java, node-serialize, .NET (row 21b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 saw the data-tamper form (unsigned base64url JSON `state` described by a format guide; role -> administrator). Sequel planner: recognise base64 blobs gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP serialize, length-prefixed strings -> fix s:N when editing), rO0 (Java), AAEAAAD (.NET BinaryFormatter), `_$$ND_FUNC$$_` (node-serialize), YAML `!!python`; first rewrite data fields (role/isAdmin/user) keeping the format's own \n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic and race conditions (row 26; reset tokens seen D17 -> sequels in auth-flow gap)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 opened multi-step flows (request -> redeem). Remaining: numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action (redeem, transfer, vote), step reordering in a checkout/approval flow. Read every guide/inventory JSON for the steps. No credential guessing. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped c\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .js\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"FIXED on D19-D20 (cal. 26): the answer-first worker promoted the plugin during the single (45 s grace at CORRECT, commit 4715290f) -> both Time Trials (10.2 s, 15.1 s) and both Mastery runs (4/4, 13-16 s) first try, the first new-class TTs to pass since D14. Before that TT went solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT start; D16 Mastery 3/4 with the plugin still `.tmp`). Keep: if a single needs >~90 s, gate \n  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.appl\n  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialect\n  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, templ\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Par\n  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-sequels\", \"concept\": \"command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind, argument injection (row 10b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 was the plain form (`ls -ld <path>` with stdout echoed; `;` worked once percent-encoded). Sequel planner, input = param name (input_parameter / `<x>_required`) + example value: separators %3B, %0a, %26%26, %7C, $(..), backticks, ${IFS} for spaces, quotes-split (c''at), wildcard paths (/run/hunt*/obj*); argument injection when the value is an argument not a shell string (`--output=/app/static/x`, `-exec cat {} ;` \n  {\"id\": \"graphql-batch-alias-mutation\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL sequels: aliases, batched arrays, mutations without authz, introspection off (row 23b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 was the plain form (introspection on, one resolver skipped the field check). Sequel planner from the schema: alias the protected field across every arg-taking Query field (a1:case(id:..){..} a2:...), JSON array batching [{query},{query}], mutations (updateX/setRole/assign) reachable without authz followed by the read, node(id:)/Relay global ids (base64 'Type:id'), fragments on interfaces/unions \n  {\"id\": \"crlf-header-injection\", \"concept\": \"CRLF / response-header injection (row 42)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params reflected into Location / Set-Cookie / custom headers (redirect targets, language, filename in Content-Disposition): %0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20role=admin, %0d%0aX-Debug:1, double CRLF to inject a body; also %E5%98%8A%E5%98%8D unicode CRLF. Then re-request the secondary route with the injected cookie. Parser: injected header in the raw response + proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte bl\n  {\"id\": \"known-vulnerable-component\", \"concept\": \"version disclosure -> a documented weakness of that exact component (row 46, OWASP A06)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched Top-10 area. Recon parser: version strings in headers (Server, X-Powered-By), /version, /health, /actuator/info, footer, package.json/composer.lock/requirements exposed via backups; map to a small local table of training-kit-style weaknesses (debug console routes, default admin route, deprecated param that skips the check) and emit only requests against the documented route/param. No exploit downlo\n  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ldap-xpath-injection\", \"concept\": \"LDAP / XPath injection (row 43)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Login or directory search over LDAP/XML: `*`, `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`, `admin)(&)`; XPath `' or '1'='1`, `'] | //* | //*['`, count()/string-length() oracles bounded to the proof alphabet. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"log-injection-forging\", \"concept\": \"log injection / forged audit entries (row 47, OWASP A09)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An audit/log route (secondary_route audit-<hex6> recurred D13/D17) that records user input and is later trusted by an approver/bot: plant `%0a` / `\\\\r\\\\n` forged lines ('[admin] approved <id>'), JSON-log key injection (\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"admin\\\"), or XSS for a bot-viewed log page; then GET the audit/secondary route. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0bf25a0-cb46-44e8-a6ad-aa115823f759","uuid":"b21e2505-517e-4234-b549-6499dc7b2a50","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:07:51.164Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D21-D28 at ~2-3 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\nstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\nraised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). Aft\n  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing a\n  {\"id\": \"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\", \"concept\": \"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a\n  {\"id\": \"webhook-signature-sequels\", \"concept\": \"webhook sequels: HMAC-signed events with a leaked/weak secret, replay, provider allowlist (row 44b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 'Trust the Webhook' was the unsigned form (clues event_type + owner_scope as body values; narrow bodies -> webhook_rejected; an alias-union JSON with role/source/trust flags -> forged_event_consumed). Signed sequel planner: read signature header names from errors/guides (X-Hub-Signature-256 'sha256=<hex>', X-Signature, X-Webhook-Signature, Stripe-Signature 't=..,v1=..', Svix 'v1,<b64>'), compu\n  {\"id\": \"alias-union-body-builder\", \"concept\": \"one JSON body carrying every clue value under every plausible alias + privilege/trust flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 lost ~60 s across three workers bisecting ~30 narrow bodies against a sink whose only error was webhook_rejected; the answer-first worker's kitchen-sink body landed first try in single/TT/Mastery. Pure builder: input = clue JSON (minus route keys) + optional guide sample; output = ordered list of JSON bodies: (1) union body: each value under its key and aliases (event_type/type/event/kind/action/topic/\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves \n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value lad\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 \n  {\"id\": \"websocket-authz\", \"concept\": \"WebSocket / alternate transport skips the REST authz (row 41)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18's prompt: 'Vary the protocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline' -- the same protected object reached via another transport. Planner: find ws:// / wss:// / socket.io / SSE / JSON-RPC endpoints in inline JS and clues; build the handshake (Origin same/foreign/null for CSWSH) and send the protected read (protected_reference) as a message; also JSON-RPC {method, params} over POST and REST<->GraphQL equivalents of t\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<all\n  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"native / signed serialization sequels: pickle, PHP, Java, node-serialize, .NET (row 21b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 saw the data-tamper form (unsigned base64url JSON `state` described by a format guide; role -> administrator). Sequel planner: recognise base64 blobs gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP serialize, length-prefixed strings -> fix s:N when editing), rO0 (Java), AAEAAAD (.NET BinaryFormatter), `_$$ND_FUNC$$_` (node-serialize), YAML `!!python`; first rewrite data fields (role/isAdmin/user) keeping the format's own \n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic and race conditions (row 26; reset tokens seen D17 -> sequels in auth-flow gap)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 opened multi-step flows (request -> redeem). Remaining: numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action (redeem, transfer, vote), step reordering in a checkout/approval flow. Read every guide/inventory JSON for the steps. No credential guessing. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped c\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .js\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"FIXED on D19-D20 (cal. 26): the answer-first worker promoted the plugin during the single (45 s grace at CORRECT, commit 4715290f) -> both Time Trials (10.2 s, 15.1 s) and both Mastery runs (4/4, 13-16 s) first try, the first new-class TTs to pass since D14. Before that TT went solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT start; D16 Mastery 3/4 with the plugin still `.tmp`). Keep: if a single needs >~90 s, gate \n  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.appl\n  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialect\n  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, templ\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Par\n  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-sequels\", \"concept\": \"command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind, argument injection (row 10b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 was the plain form (`ls -ld <path>` with stdout echoed; `;` worked once percent-encoded). Sequel planner, input = param name (input_parameter / `<x>_required`) + example value: separators %3B, %0a, %26%26, %7C, $(..), backticks, ${IFS} for spaces, quotes-split (c''at), wildcard paths (/run/hunt*/obj*); argument injection when the value is an argument not a shell string (`--output=/app/static/x`, `-exec cat {} ;` \n  {\"id\": \"graphql-batch-alias-mutation\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL sequels: aliases, batched arrays, mutations without authz, introspection off (row 23b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 was the plain form (introspection on, one resolver skipped the field check). Sequel planner from the schema: alias the protected field across every arg-taking Query field (a1:case(id:..){..} a2:...), JSON array batching [{query},{query}], mutations (updateX/setRole/assign) reachable without authz followed by the read, node(id:)/Relay global ids (base64 'Type:id'), fragments on interfaces/unions \n  {\"id\": \"crlf-header-injection\", \"concept\": \"CRLF / response-header injection (row 42)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params reflected into Location / Set-Cookie / custom headers (redirect targets, language, filename in Content-Disposition): %0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20role=admin, %0d%0aX-Debug:1, double CRLF to inject a body; also %E5%98%8A%E5%98%8D unicode CRLF. Then re-request the secondary route with the injected cookie. Parser: injected header in the raw response + proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte bl\n  {\"id\": \"known-vulnerable-component\", \"concept\": \"version disclosure -> a documented weakness of that exact component (row 46, OWASP A06)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Untouched Top-10 area. Recon parser: version strings in headers (Server, X-Powered-By), /version, /health, /actuator/info, footer, package.json/composer.lock/requirements exposed via backups; map to a small local table of training-kit-style weaknesses (debug console routes, default admin route, deprecated param that skips the check) and emit only requests against the documented route/param. No exploit downlo\n  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ldap-xpath-injection\", \"concept\": \"LDAP / XPath injection (row 43)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Login or directory search over LDAP/XML: `*`, `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`, `admin)(&)`; XPath `' or '1'='1`, `'] | //* | //*['`, count()/string-length() oracles bounded to the proof alphabet. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"log-injection-forging\", \"concept\": \"log injection / forged audit entries (row 47, OWASP A09)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An audit/log route (secondary_route audit-<hex6> recurred D13/D17) that records user input and is later trusted by an approver/bot: plant `%0a` / `\\\\r\\\\n` forged lines ('[admin] approved <id>'), JSON-log key injection (\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"admin\\\"), or XSS for a bot-viewed log page; then GET the audit/secondary route. Parser: proof regex / evidence.\"}\n]\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TpUiUgaDryaxMKTQCSE8e2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
