lvers for the same prompt dependence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"path-verb-normalization-bypass\", \"concept\": \"HTTP verb / method override and path-normalisation authz bypass (rows 16, 17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D23 took the header half of the old 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass' gap (seen). The other two classic 403-bypass families remain and fit a 'protected path' kit (D23's prompt: 'stroll down the protected path'). Pure planner for a route that 401/403/405s: methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS/TRACE + X-HTTP-Method-Override / X-Method-Override / _method=; path variants /ROUTE upper-case, trailing /, /., //route, /./route, /route;/, /route..;/, %2e/%2f/%61 single-char encodings, trailing ?/#, X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with a harmless base path. Parser: proof regex; diff status/body against the baseline 403 and stop at the first 200 with evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"business-logic-tamper\", \"concept\": \"business-logic sequels: negative/huge amounts, price in the body, coupon replay, step reorder (row 26b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D21 showed a ledger kit (feature POST spends credits, secondary audits the balance). Sibling flaws a sequel day would use: quantity/amount -1, 0, 1e9, 0.0001, strings ('1e3'), a client-sent price/total field, a redeem/coupon token replayed or applied twice sequentially, a checkout/approval step called out of order. Planner input = guide/clue JSON + one observed request body; output = <= 12 single-change JSON bodies, GET secondary after each. GET-only recon first (one-shot state, see race-burst-first-dispatch). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sse-socketio-transport\", \"concept\": \"other real-time transports: SSE, socket.io/engine.io, JSON-RPC, per-message WS authz (row 41b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D22 was the plain WS form (Origin present + ?stream=<stream_reference> -> first frame has the proof). Sequel planner reusing lib/web/handlers/day27_web_socket_to_me.py's stdlib client: SSE (GET with Accept: text/event-stream, parse `data:` lines, stream id as ?stream=/?channel=/Last-Event-ID), socket.io v4 (GET /socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=polling -> sid, then 40 / 42[\\\"subscribe\\\",ref] over polling or WS upgrade), per-message authz (open own stream, send {\\\"subscribe\\\"|\\\"join\\\"|\\\"stream\\\": protected ref}), Origin variants (own, foreign, null) when the handshake is origin-checked. Parser: proof regex over every frame/event.\"}\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in byid\norder = [g['id'] for g in gaps if g['id'] in byid]\n# insert new p1 notes after 'record-target-responses', prebuilds near top\nout = []\nfor i in order:\n    out.append(byid[i])\n    if i == 'codify-before-tt':\n        pass\nout = [g for g in out]\n# put codify-before-tt + the two notes right after enable-web-prebuild-lane\nfirst = [byid['enable-web-prebuild-lane'], new[0], new[1], byid['codify-before-tt']]\nrest = [g for g in out if g['id'] not in ('enable-web-prebuild-lane', 'codify-before-tt')]\np1 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 1]\n# new prebuilds among p1 after jwt\nidx = next(k for k, g in enumerate(p1) if g['id'] == 'jwt-session-forge') + 1\np1[idx:idx] = [byid['cache-host-header'], byid['cors-misconfig-probe'], new[2], new[3]]\np1 = list(dict.fromkeys(g['id'] for g in p1))\np1 = [byid.get(i) or next(n for n in new if n['id'] == i) for i in p1]\np2 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 2 and g['id'] not in ('cache-host-header', 'cors-misconfig-probe')] + [new[4]]\np3 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 3 and g['id'] not in ('cache-host-header', 'cors-misconfig-probe')]\nfinal = first + p1 + p2 + p3\nids = [g['id'] for g in final]\nassert len(ids) == len(set(ids)), ids\nassert all(set(g) == {'id', 'concept', 'priority', 'action', 'detail'} for g in final)\nbody = \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in final) + \"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\n