verspent + credits, 409 credit_unavailable                        then GET secondary (UNSOLVED: success shape unknown)\nstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required,      -> WS stream (D22)    -> WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin: <target> (none = 403);\n  \"upgraded to websockets ... never meant for you\"                              proof in the first server text frame (stdlib socket+ssl client)\ndeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> GET feature with X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (then X-Real-IP, Forwarded:\n  + evaluated_client, \"whatever the proxy whispers\"                             for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP); evaluated_client must flip\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"SSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/... \"localhost only\" -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\"; ws:// in JS          -> shadow API / WS    -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"SSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...; Host/X-Forwarded-Host in links -> poison\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\"; EventSource/socket.io -> shadow API / SSE  -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20 -> TT first\ntry; D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23 -> TT\nfirst try; D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22 TT solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\"\"\")\n\n# --- gaps JSON\nm = re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```', s, re.S)\ngaps = json.loads(m.group(1))\nbyid = {g['id']: g for g in gaps}\nfor dead in ('websocket-authz', 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass', 'logic-race-reset'):\n    del byid[dead]\ndef setp(i, pr, extra=None):\n    byid[i]['priority'] = pr\n    if extra:\n        byid[i]['detail'] = extra + ' ' + byid[i]['detail']\nsetp('codify-before-tt', 1, \"REGRESSED on cal. 27: D22 Socket to Me's handler landed 21:02:33, 20 s after the TT solve began (21:01:59-21:02:13) -> TT solver_incomplete (live worker CORRECT ~40 s after ready). D23's handler landed before TT -> 10.5 s first try.\")\nsetp('cache-host-header', 1, \"Raised after D23 (proxy-trust day): the same 'trusted proxy' kit with another header family is the natural sequel -- X-Forwarded-Host / X-Host / X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL one at a time against the feature route, and Host-poisoned reset/callback links. Reuse D23's error shape: a JSON error that echoes what the app evaluated (`evaluated_client`) tells which header bound.\")\nsetp('cors-misconfig-probe', 1, \"Raised after D22: the WS handshake was gated only on an Origin header being PRESENT (own or foreign accepted) -- the origin-trust family is live in this kit.\")\nsetp('webhook-signature-sequels', 2, \"Lowered after cal. 27: D21-D23 were all new concepts, not D19/D20 sequels.\")\nsetp('ssrf-filter-bypass', 2, \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19).\")\nsetp('deserialization-gadgets', 2, \"Lowered after cal. 27 (new concepts outrank sequels since D19; JWT stays priority 1).\")\nbyid['jwt-session-forge']['detail'] = \"Still unseen after D23 -- the biggest remaining session/integrity class. \" + byid['jwt-session-forge']['detail']\nnew = [\n  {\"id\": \"race-burst-first-dispatch\", \"concept\": \"one-shot race targets must get the concurrent burst before ANY sequential POST (row 26)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n   \"detail\": \"D21 Double Spent single was never solved: at the workers' first GET the secondary already said credit_not_overspent credits:0 and every POST -> 409 credit_unavailable (sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2, 24x barrier). The race_bisect / prior-solver dry run ran 16 s on the fresh target (13:00:43-13:00:59) and its default ladder + D12/D13/D19 handlers POST to feature_route, which spends the one credit. Owner of lib/web + hctf: (1) promote challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py (GET gate on the secondary, barrier-synced ~24 POST {} burst, GET secondary) as lib/web/handlers/day27_web_double_spent.py; (2) in lib/web candidates(), when any GET body says credit_not_overspent / credits / balance / remaining, run ONLY the race handler first; (3) race_bisect / dry runs must be GET-only on web targets (or skip web). Matters for every future Mastery that deals a D21 target. Record the success effect spelling when it lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-prompt-free-defaults\", \"concept\": \"earlier-day web solvers must not derive parameters from the Mastery prompt\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n   \"detail\": \"Cal. 27: both Mastery runs (D22, D23) went 4/5 -- proof-4 was a D04 Stay in Your Directory target (PHP+Apache, no /api/clues, `handbook.php?doc=triage.php` | `notes.php?doc=..`, proof in <article>). challenges/day20/web-stay-in-your-directory/solver/solve.py lfi() takes its read path from the prompt text (regex for /run|/etc|..) and otherwise uses /flag.txt; the Mastery prompt is today's, so it never tried /run/huntress/objective.txt. Fix: always include /run/huntress/objective.txt (and /run/huntress/config.json for classification) in the path list. Audit the other earlier-day solvers for the same prompt dependence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"path-verb-normalization-bypass\", \"concept\": \"HTTP verb / method override and path-normalisation authz bypass (rows 16, 17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D23 took the header half of the old 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass' gap (seen). The other two classic 403-bypass families remain and fit a 'protected path' kit (D23's prompt: 'stroll down the protected path'). Pure planner for a route that 401/403/405s: methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS/TRACE + X-HTTP-Method-Override / X-Method-Override / _method=; path variants /ROUTE upper-case, trailing /, /., //route, /./route, /route;/, /route..;/, %2e/%2f/%61 single-char encodings, trailing ?/#, X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with a harmless base path. Parser: proof regex; diff status/body against the baseline 403 and stop at the first 200 with evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"business-logic-tamper\", \"concept\": \"business-logic sequels: negative/huge amounts, price in the body, coupon replay, step reorder (row 26b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D21 showed a ledger kit (feature POST spends credits, secondary audits the balance). Sibling flaws a sequel day would use: quantity/amount -1, 0, 1e9, 0.0001, strings ('1e3'), a client-sent price/total field, a redeem/coupon token replayed or applied twice sequentially, a checkout/approval step called out of order. Planner input = guide/clue JSON + one observed request body; output = <= 12 single-change JSON bodies, GET secondary after each. GET-only recon first (one-shot state, see race-burst-first-dispatch). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sse-socketio-transport\", \"concept\": \"other real-time transports: SSE, socket.io/engine.io, JSON-RPC, per-message WS authz (row 41b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n   \"detail\": \"D22 was the plain WS form (Origin present + ?stream=<stream_reference> -> first frame has the proof). Sequel planner reusing lib/web/handlers/day27_web_socket_to_me.py's stdlib client: SSE (GET with Accept: text/event-stream, parse `data:` lines, stream id as ?stream=/?channel=/Last-Event-ID), socket.io v4 (GET /socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=polling -> sid, then 40 / 42[\\\"subscribe\\\",ref] over polling or WS upgrade), per-message authz (open own stream, send {\\\"subscribe\\\"|\\\"join\\\"|\\\"stream\\\": protected ref}), Origin variants (own, foreign, null) when the handshake is origin-checked. Parser: proof regex over every frame/event.\"}\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in byid\norder = [g['id'] for g in gaps if g['id'] in byid]\n# insert new p1 notes after 'record-target-responses', prebuilds near top\nout = []\nfor i in order:\n    out.append(byid[i])\n    if i == 'codify-before-tt':\n        pass\nout = [g for g in out]\n# put codify-before-tt + the two notes right after enable-web-prebuild-lane\nfirst = [byid['enable-web-prebuild-lane'], new[0], new[1], byid['codify-before-tt']]\nrest = [g for g in out if g['id'] not in ('enable-web-prebuild-lane', 'codify-before-tt')]\np1 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 1]\n# new prebuilds among p1 after jwt\nidx = next(k for k, g in enumerate(p1) if g['id'] == 'jwt-session-forge') + 1\np1[idx:idx] = [byid['cache-host-header'], byid['cors-misconfig-probe'], new[2], new[3]]\np1 = list(dict.fromkeys(g['id'] for g in p1))\np1 = [byid.get(i) or next(n for n in new if n['id'] == i) for i in p1]\np2 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 2 and g['id'] not in ('cache-host-header', 'cors-misconfig-probe')] + [new[4]]\np3 = [g for g in rest if g['priority'] == 3 and g['id'] not in ('cache-host-header', 'cors-misconfig-probe')]\nfinal = first + p1 + p2 + p3\nids = [g['id'] for g in final]\nassert len(ids) == len(set(ids)), ids\nassert all(set(g) == {'id', 'concept', 'priority', 'action', 'detail'} for g in final)\nbody = \"[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in final) + \"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\ns = s[:m.start(1)] + body + s[m.end(1):]\n\n# gaps preamble\nrep(\"\"\"Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Dropped after D23 (cal. 27): `websocket-authz` (seen D22 -> `sse-socketio-transport`), `header-trust-verb-path-bypass`\n(header half seen D23 -> `path-verb-normalization-bypass`), `logic-race-reset` (race seen D21, unsolved ->\n`race-burst-first-dispatch` note + `business-logic-tamper`). Added: `mastery-prompt-free-defaults`. Raised to 1:\n`cache-host-header`, `cors-misconfig-probe`, `codify-before-tt` (regressed on D22). Lowered to 2: webhook / SSRF /\ndeserialization sequels (new concepts beat sequels since D19). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D21-D28 at ~2-3 lane-days per day).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D24-D29 at ~2 lane-days per day).\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint(len(final), sum(1 for g in final if g['action'] == 'prebuild'))\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/atlas_edit.py"}}}
